# social, one member: an invite that reads, bears cells and speaks, and the member's own stream
#
# `room welcome $ROOM SUBJECT --template social` binds $MEMBER to SUBJECT and
# runs these lines as you, the founder (PLACE §2.3 (a)). You bear the
# member's stream into the room, pay for it and own it (a birth into a room is
# owned by its creator); its law lets nobody but $MEMBER write or append to it,
# you included. The member speaks in it with the invite (append under the
# room), so a kick ends that too. Hand the member the invite `publish` prints
# (export ID shows it again).

room invite $ROOM-invite-$MEMBER $ROOM $MEMBER --verbs observe,place,append
submit $ROOM-invite-$MEMBER
publish $ROOM-invite-$MEMBER
create $ROOM/stream-$MEMBER stream 'any [ not (verb in {write, append}), subject == $MEMBER ]' --in $ROOM
